[size=12pt][b]Where Core is ahead, and why[/b][/size]

[table]
[tr][td][b]module[/b][/td][td][b]Core[/b][/td][td][b]bmc[/b][/td][td][b]ratio[/b][/td][td][b]why[/b][/td][/tr]
[tr][td]BIP324 ECDH[/td][td]21.0 us[/td][td]30.9 us[/td][td][b]1.5x slower[/b][/td][td]a constant-time GLV window over complete formulas (84 ns a double, 117 an add) vs libsecp256k1's ecmult_const; 3.2x on 09-27[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]BIP324 packet AEAD, 64 B[/td][td]2.26 ns/B[/td][td]3.65 ns/B[/td][td][b]1.6x slower[/b][/td][td]three single ChaCha20 blocks per small packet: their latency is the row[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]CheckBlock, block 413,567[/td][td]367 us[/td][td]585 us[/td][td][b]1.6x slower[/b][/td][td]Core does more per block (see tests/bench_checkblock.c); 1.8x in the morning[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]GCS filter header hash[/td][td]62 us[/td][td]95 us[/td][td][b]1.5x slower[/b][/td][td]SHA-256d over the 263 KB encoded filter plus the header link[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]taproot script-path verify[/td][td]36.0 us[/td][td]49.3 us[/td][td][b]1.4x slower[/b][/td][td]ours spends a 2-leaf tree; Core a 1-leaf[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Poly1305, 64 B[/td][td]0.44 ns/B[/td][td]0.54 ns/B[/td][td][b]1.2x slower[/b][/td][td]per-packet setup[/td][/tr]
